","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Walk/run blending passed a raw float through shared speed and cycle\ninterpolation, then admitted the same factor again for flight height.\nBoth interpolation methods now accept the existing `UnitInterval` type.\nLocomotion admits its run factor once and reuses it across those operations;\nthe low-endurance speed producer also supplies an admitted blend.\n\nThe endurance smoothstep result is clamped to its intended `[0, 1]` range\nbefore admission. `SpeedError` derives its error implementation and carries\n`FractionError`; animation uses its existing fraction-error conversion.\nRelated: #780 and #726.\n\n## Validation\n\nIndependent Code, Rule and Comment source reviews found no actionable issues.\nHosted checks are pending. The workflow now executes the four existing\nmovement-speed tests and rejects empty or failing results.\nNo tests, cases, helpers, assertions or doctests were added.\n\n## Implementation context\n\nThe shared core `UnitInterval` remains the sole fraction owner. Scalar values\nare extracted inside the interpolation kernels and at the complementary\nbounce calculation. This completes both speed callers and the cycle caller\nwithout a raw-float overload.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T04:45:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T04:45:30Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2dab4201e1899598b55dd34d4ae1d55a2dc6a706","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"adventure-simulator-group:codex/780-type-interpolation-fractions","ref":"codex/780-type-interpolation-fractions","repo":{"id":1049441561,"node_id":"R_kgDOPo01GQ","name":"fabelgeist","full_name":"adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist","owner":{"login":"adventure-simulator-group","id":230064938,"node_id":"O_kgDODbaDKg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230064938?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://